{
 "_doc": [
  "Only two kinds of hand entries live here; every other status is COMPUTED by scan.py from the sources:",
  "1) not_applicable: na = 'linux' (Linux-only interface/infrastructure) or 'hw' (hardware the B580 does not have) + a one-line reason.",
  "2) missing: only with a machine-checked proof: 'refuse' regexes that must match in our sources (a feature refused with an error)",
  "   and/or 'absent' tokens (names or register offsets) that must not occur in our sources. If the proof fails, the file is 'unverified'.",
  "Computed statuses: ported = every upstream function (or, for headers without functions, every #define) occurs in our sources;",
  "partial = some do; unverified = none do and no proof of absence. Mesa: upstream/patched/ours/not_built from git diff + compile_commands.json.",
  "Paths: xe/... drivers/gpu/drm/xe, display/... drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display, uapi/xe_drm.h, mesa/... = Mesa src/, ours/... = repo user/.",
  "n/a 'hw' rules carry 'future': the other Intel GPU family the file serves (future target); n/a 'old' = pre-Gen12 platforms outside xe (not needed)."
 ],
